## Vendored upstream launcher

`vendor/upstream-install-and-test.sh` is upstream's launcher at the pinned tag
(upstream copyright retained in the file), vendored so the shell pins the exact
bytes it runs — **plus one recorded local patch**: a portability fix replacing
`tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]'` with `tr 'A-Z' 'a-z'`, because busybox `tr` has no
character classes and the original turned `Linux` into `Linlx`, 404ing every
release-asset URL on OpenWrt. That patch is offered upstream as a separate PR and
is carried here until it lands. This is the ONLY difference from the pinned tag.

The patch is part of what is pinned: `scripts/build-pinned-upstream.sh` step 6
asserts the composed tree, the recorded sha256 and the vendored file all agree,
and `install.sh` aborts if the vendored bytes do not match
`scripts/upstream-launcher.sha256`.

